1
00:00:00,156 --> 00:00:02,356
(Hwanggeum Apparel)

2
00:00:02,426 --> 00:00:03,596
(Episode 4)

3
00:00:03,656 --> 00:00:05,896
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

4
00:00:19,276 --> 00:00:21,446
My niece must be very busy.

5
00:00:21,876 --> 00:00:23,046
I haven't heard from you.

6
00:00:32,986 --> 00:00:36,196
I will see you in one hour at the place we last met.

7
00:00:40,766 --> 00:00:42,396
(CEO Jeon Jin Hee)

8
00:00:46,266 --> 00:00:47,636
Yes, CEO Jeon.

9
00:00:47,706 --> 00:00:49,206
Tell Assistant Manager Kang from Product Planning...

10
00:00:49,206 --> 00:00:51,176
that we have dinner tomorrow...

11
00:00:51,576 --> 00:00:53,906
and that someone I want to introduce will be joining us,

12
00:00:53,976 --> 00:00:55,146
so she should be aware.

13
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:56,846
You know the time and place, right?

14
00:00:57,476 --> 00:01:00,186
Yes. I will deliver your message exactly as you said.

15
00:01:04,386 --> 00:01:06,926
Let's see if she is just playing dumb...

16
00:01:08,056 --> 00:01:09,296
or if she is truly cunning.

17
00:01:43,956 --> 00:01:45,126
Goodness...

18
00:01:45,596 --> 00:01:47,196
That's a nice car.

19
00:01:47,866 --> 00:01:49,666
Jin Sook!

20
00:01:58,906 --> 00:02:00,876
It seems you still haven't quit drinking.

21
00:02:01,876 --> 00:02:05,116
I don't have any friends other than that.

22
00:02:05,246 --> 00:02:07,786
What do you want? Money again, I assume.

23
00:02:08,786 --> 00:02:12,156
A nice property came up in Seongsu-dong.

24
00:02:14,056 --> 00:02:15,386
Have you not quit gambling either?

25
00:02:17,926 --> 00:02:18,926
What?

26
00:02:20,066 --> 00:02:22,466
That has been your lover your whole life.

27
00:02:24,596 --> 00:02:27,336
I'll send you my account number, so wire it by tomorrow.

28
00:02:32,446 --> 00:02:33,746
This is the last time.

29
00:02:36,976 --> 00:02:39,316
That's what I want too, you brat.

30
00:02:41,486 --> 00:02:44,916
She is still the same. So rude.

31
00:03:05,376 --> 00:03:06,406
Disgusting.

32
00:03:36,736 --> 00:03:38,176
(My Son Do Yun)

33
00:03:39,906 --> 00:03:41,006
(My Son Do Yun)

34
00:03:43,216 --> 00:03:44,246
Hey, son.

35
00:03:46,786 --> 00:03:50,286
Mom, I just woke up and saw your text.

36
00:03:50,956 --> 00:03:53,426
But you want me to pick up clothes at the department store?

37
00:03:53,926 --> 00:03:55,996
There is an important gathering tomorrow evening.

38
00:03:56,056 --> 00:03:58,526
I ordered them under your name,

39
00:03:58,596 --> 00:04:00,626
so go try them on and pick what you like.

40
00:04:02,066 --> 00:04:03,296
What kind of gathering is it?

41
00:04:03,936 --> 00:04:05,196
You will see when you get there.

42
00:04:05,706 --> 00:04:07,066
Are you feeling okay?

43
00:04:07,736 --> 00:04:09,676
You should go to the hospital and get an IV drip.

44
00:04:10,176 --> 00:04:12,136
I was just tired from a lack of sleep.

45
00:04:12,576 --> 00:04:13,676
I'm fine now.

46
00:04:14,006 --> 00:04:15,106
That's a relief.

47
00:04:16,316 --> 00:04:17,676
I will see you at home tonight.

48
00:04:18,076 --> 00:04:19,086
Okay.

49
00:04:31,126 --> 00:04:32,196
Goodness.

50
00:04:42,066 --> 00:04:45,076
What's going on with you? Skipping work and all.

51
00:04:45,136 --> 00:04:47,206
I know. I guess days like this happen.

52
00:04:48,046 --> 00:04:51,116
But what are you hiding behind your back, Se Na?

53
00:04:52,986 --> 00:04:53,986
Ta-da.

54
00:04:54,646 --> 00:04:55,916
Hey, put that away right now.

55
00:04:56,986 --> 00:04:59,086
What do you think? Does it not make you excited?

56
00:04:59,156 --> 00:05:00,556
I said, put it away.

57
00:05:01,826 --> 00:05:04,426
I designed and custom-ordered it myself.

58
00:05:04,826 --> 00:05:06,796
Do Yun, don't be like that. Take a close look.

59
00:05:07,526 --> 00:05:10,166
Does your company have any plans to launch an underwear brand?

60
00:05:10,696 --> 00:05:13,266
If you do, buy my designs. Please?

61
00:05:14,006 --> 00:05:15,166
- Why you... - Ouch.

62
00:05:15,236 --> 00:05:17,876
I told you to prepare to study abroad, not do useless things.

63
00:05:18,206 --> 00:05:19,646
You are still wet behind the ears.

64
00:05:19,846 --> 00:05:21,976
Well, if I dry out, I will die.

65
00:05:22,446 --> 00:05:25,416
Don't be like that and take a serious look.

66
00:05:26,846 --> 00:05:27,886
Get lost.

67
00:05:32,926 --> 00:05:35,186
He just looks down on me because I'm young.

68
00:05:45,536 --> 00:05:48,836
There will definitely come a day when you'll find this useful.

69
00:05:49,436 --> 00:05:50,706
When I get famous?

70
00:05:51,376 --> 00:05:53,346
You won't be able to buy it even if you want to.

71
00:05:54,646 --> 00:05:56,916
I'll shove my early works right in your face.

72
00:06:05,216 --> 00:06:06,286
That's the taste.

73
00:06:07,926 --> 00:06:09,726
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

74
00:06:09,926 --> 00:06:12,896
What? Su Ah's mom isn't home?

75
00:06:14,296 --> 00:06:15,426
They moved.

76
00:06:15,766 --> 00:06:17,096
What are you talking about?

77
00:06:17,536 --> 00:06:19,806
They moved? Why?

78
00:06:20,566 --> 00:06:21,966
And without saying a word?

79
00:06:22,676 --> 00:06:23,706
Tell me about it.

80
00:06:28,346 --> 00:06:31,476
Ri Ja, don't say a word to Mother.

81
00:06:31,546 --> 00:06:35,286
I should find out what on earth is going on before telling her.

82
00:06:35,516 --> 00:06:38,286
There is no need to worry her. She has high blood pressure.

83
00:06:39,086 --> 00:06:40,086
Okay.

84
00:06:40,156 --> 00:06:42,086
(Mi Mi's Chicken Soup)

85
00:06:43,096 --> 00:06:46,626
They're so weird. How could they just move...

86
00:06:46,696 --> 00:06:49,066
without discussing it when they know who bought them the house?

87
00:06:51,636 --> 00:06:52,936
It's unbelievable.

88
00:06:53,536 --> 00:06:55,736
Why is there never a peaceful day?

89
00:06:56,136 --> 00:06:58,776
Gosh, so you just brought it back?

90
00:06:58,836 --> 00:07:01,606
You should have at least left it at Dae Chi's officetel.

91
00:07:02,206 --> 00:07:04,416
He told me not to call because he's busy.

92
00:07:04,646 --> 00:07:06,586
And does he even eat at home?

93
00:07:07,616 --> 00:07:10,886
That's true. He goes to work at dawn...

94
00:07:10,956 --> 00:07:12,486
and comes home when the stars are out.

95
00:07:14,086 --> 00:07:18,026
Working for a large corporation really drains a person, right?

96
00:07:19,026 --> 00:07:20,526
But what's going on with Su Ah's family?

97
00:07:22,366 --> 00:07:25,566
They didn't ruin the Taekwondo studio too, did they?

98
00:07:26,706 --> 00:07:29,276
There you go again. Always jinxing things.

99
00:07:29,806 --> 00:07:32,376
All right. Sorry.

100
00:07:36,276 --> 00:07:41,016
Mi Seon and Gang Nam like these best.

101
00:07:42,216 --> 00:07:43,216
How sad...

102
00:08:28,696 --> 00:08:29,696
Mother?

103
00:08:42,846 --> 00:08:45,076
Mother, what medicine are you taking?

104
00:08:45,646 --> 00:08:47,186
Is something making you feel uncomfortable?

105
00:08:48,316 --> 00:08:51,186
It feels like someone is poking this side of my head...

106
00:08:51,956 --> 00:08:56,096
with a whole pack of needles.

107
00:08:57,956 --> 00:09:00,496
Oh my, is Gang Nam's family doing well?

108
00:09:01,866 --> 00:09:04,766
What happened to the container? Why did you only bring the cloth?

109
00:09:05,636 --> 00:09:07,206
If you gave them the side dishes,

110
00:09:07,266 --> 00:09:09,236
shouldn't you have brought the empty container back?

111
00:09:10,176 --> 00:09:14,076
Oh, well, they weren't home. So I just came back.

112
00:09:14,476 --> 00:09:17,076
Oh, I left the container in the fridge at the store, Mother.

113
00:09:17,146 --> 00:09:18,376
Oh, you.

114
00:09:19,386 --> 00:09:22,286
I guess your brain doesn't work as well as you get older.

115
00:09:23,486 --> 00:09:27,026
If they weren't there, you could have left it at the security office.

116
00:09:27,086 --> 00:09:30,026
Why would you carry it all the way back and hurt your shoulders?

117
00:09:31,256 --> 00:09:32,256
I know, right?

118
00:09:37,936 --> 00:09:38,936
Mi Mi.

119
00:09:40,836 --> 00:09:41,906
Yes?

120
00:09:42,436 --> 00:09:46,706
I just keep liking you more and more.

121
00:09:47,746 --> 00:09:49,676
The more I see you, the more I like you.

122
00:09:51,146 --> 00:09:53,346
Mother, why are you saying this all of a sudden?

123
00:09:54,646 --> 00:09:56,686
What do you like so much about me?

124
00:09:57,016 --> 00:09:59,156
My looks? My vitality?

125
00:09:59,216 --> 00:10:01,026
Well, when I hear other grandmothers talk,

126
00:10:01,086 --> 00:10:02,556
they say their daughters-in-law don't even ask...

127
00:10:02,626 --> 00:10:05,696
and are just busy throwing away all their mothers-in-law's things.

128
00:10:06,066 --> 00:10:08,726
But you don't throw away a single wrapping cloth of mine carelessly,

129
00:10:08,796 --> 00:10:09,966
and for years now,

130
00:10:10,036 --> 00:10:13,306
you wash it and hang it to dry, again and again.

131
00:10:14,406 --> 00:10:17,236
I don't know how I got so lucky.

132
00:10:18,836 --> 00:10:20,606
I'll do even better, Mother.

133
00:10:34,026 --> 00:10:36,256
Manager Kang, how many outfits are there in total today?

134
00:10:36,526 --> 00:10:37,926
It's a total of six outfits.

135
00:10:38,626 --> 00:10:40,496
Please deliver them all to my house.

136
00:10:41,026 --> 00:10:42,126
Thank you.

137
00:10:42,426 --> 00:10:45,566
Once you change, I will get them ready and deliver them home.

138
00:10:45,836 --> 00:10:47,606
They will arrive by this evening.

139
00:10:48,306 --> 00:10:49,306
Thank you.

140
00:11:06,186 --> 00:11:07,186
Goodness.

141
00:11:08,126 --> 00:11:10,396
What are you doing here?

142
00:11:13,526 --> 00:11:16,036
Oh, I'm 15 minutes early.

143
00:11:16,366 --> 00:11:17,796
I should have a reservation.

144
00:11:17,866 --> 00:11:20,636
You're... Wait...

145
00:11:20,706 --> 00:11:23,706
If you don't mind me asking, what is your name...

146
00:11:23,776 --> 00:11:24,776
I am Cha Do Yun.

147
00:11:26,146 --> 00:11:28,746
What? He was a VIP at our department store?

148
00:11:29,276 --> 00:11:31,816
I couldn't sleep all night because of you.

149
00:11:31,876 --> 00:11:33,186
Because it was so unfair.

150
00:11:34,686 --> 00:11:37,386
- Oh, you had a customer. - I was just about to leave.

151
00:11:45,526 --> 00:11:46,696
Here, Da Mi.

152
00:11:47,196 --> 00:11:49,096
No, ma'am, you do this every time.

153
00:11:52,496 --> 00:11:54,706
While I am on my cruise trip,

154
00:11:54,766 --> 00:11:56,736
I won't be able to see you for two months,

155
00:11:56,806 --> 00:11:59,706
- so take care of yourself. - Thank you.

156
00:12:00,006 --> 00:12:02,346
Have a wonderful trip, and I will see you again.

157
00:12:02,946 --> 00:12:03,946
Yes, let's do that.

158
00:12:11,586 --> 00:12:12,786
Goodbye.

159
00:12:20,266 --> 00:12:22,026
Your name is...

160
00:12:22,666 --> 00:12:24,266
really Cha Do Yun...

161
00:12:25,396 --> 00:12:26,936
Yes, that's correct.

162
00:12:34,446 --> 00:12:37,046
First, how about this item?

163
00:12:38,676 --> 00:12:39,946
I will try it on first.

164
00:12:40,316 --> 00:12:42,816
But my arms and legs are a bit long.

165
00:12:44,786 --> 00:12:47,226
Sir, you can hand me your jacket.

166
00:12:48,826 --> 00:12:49,826
All right.

167
00:13:20,726 --> 00:13:21,726
What is this?

168
00:13:31,636 --> 00:13:32,766
Oh, my gosh!

169
00:13:37,636 --> 00:13:40,476
I thought it would be too short, but it fits perfectly...

170
00:13:46,846 --> 00:13:48,486
Wait, why is this here...

171
00:13:52,956 --> 00:13:53,956
Please give it to me.

172
00:13:55,326 --> 00:13:57,256
Yes, of course.

173
00:13:57,956 --> 00:14:00,096
It did come out of your pocket, sir.

174
00:14:05,736 --> 00:14:07,166
What a pervert.

175
00:14:07,466 --> 00:14:08,466
Darn it.

176
00:14:12,076 --> 00:14:14,676
Don't get the wrong idea. I'm not a weird person.

177
00:14:15,776 --> 00:14:18,176
Isn't it weird to carry around sexy women's underwear...

178
00:14:18,176 --> 00:14:19,516
in your pocket?

179
00:14:19,716 --> 00:14:21,746
First of all, I'm saying this isn't mine.

180
00:14:21,816 --> 00:14:22,956
I'm sure it's not.

181
00:14:23,016 --> 00:14:25,786
- Because it is women's underwear. - That is not what I mean.

182
00:14:25,856 --> 00:14:28,386
It's not just any woman's underwear. This belongs to...

183
00:14:28,656 --> 00:14:31,396
And the reason why this came out of my pocket is...

184
00:14:31,796 --> 00:14:34,066
I don't want to know at all, sir.

185
00:14:34,696 --> 00:14:37,836
The suit looks really good on you. Would you like to purchase this one?

186
00:14:40,206 --> 00:14:41,436
It belongs to my younger sister.

187
00:14:42,536 --> 00:14:43,636
That's even weirder.

188
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,246
Would you like to purchase it?

189
00:14:48,346 --> 00:14:49,406
If you really can't believe me,

190
00:14:49,476 --> 00:14:51,476
I can bring my sister here, and we can talk face-to-face.

191
00:14:51,476 --> 00:14:52,476
Should I?

192
00:14:52,546 --> 00:14:55,116
Sir, would you like to purchase it?

193
00:14:57,856 --> 00:15:00,226
- Sure, I will. - You can just change and come out.

194
00:15:06,026 --> 00:15:08,966
I have never seen such a crazy guy in my whole life.

195
00:15:21,106 --> 00:15:22,446
Cha Se Na.

196
00:15:22,976 --> 00:15:25,276
Just wait and see what I do to you today.

197
00:15:37,956 --> 00:15:40,766
I will pack a new one and have it delivered to your home.

198
00:15:40,826 --> 00:15:44,366
- If you wait a moment... - No, just pack this one.

199
00:15:44,436 --> 00:15:45,796
I will take it with me right now.

200
00:15:46,506 --> 00:15:47,836
Nice. Thank you.

201
00:15:48,566 --> 00:15:49,566
Yes, sir.

202
00:15:55,506 --> 00:15:57,246
(K Department Store)

203
00:16:04,516 --> 00:16:07,086
Thank you, sir. Have a good day.

204
00:16:13,226 --> 00:16:15,996
Don't ever come back. Never ever come back.

205
00:16:25,036 --> 00:16:27,246
(K Department Store)

206
00:16:29,376 --> 00:16:30,446
(Health Checkup Voucher, 3,000 dollars)

207
00:16:31,146 --> 00:16:32,976
Goodness, how much is this worth?

208
00:16:34,916 --> 00:16:36,886
One, two, three...

209
00:16:36,956 --> 00:16:38,216
It's 3,000 dollars?

210
00:16:40,786 --> 00:16:43,626
Thank you, ma'am. Thank you so much.

211
00:16:44,056 --> 00:16:46,796
I hope you only have smooth sailing on your cruise...

212
00:16:46,996 --> 00:16:49,426
and that you have nothing but bright and sunny days.

213
00:16:58,006 --> 00:16:59,236
(Mi Seon)

214
00:16:59,976 --> 00:17:02,506
Mi Seon, what happened?

215
00:17:02,576 --> 00:17:04,246
If you say that and then keep ignoring my calls,

216
00:17:04,246 --> 00:17:05,376
what am I supposed to do?

217
00:17:05,646 --> 00:17:07,386
Let's meet after work, Da Mi.

218
00:17:07,746 --> 00:17:09,586
I have something to tell you in private.

219
00:17:13,356 --> 00:17:16,026
Mr. Kang Dae Chi. Avoiding my calls all day...

220
00:17:16,086 --> 00:17:17,826
isn't going to solve the problem, is it?

221
00:17:18,856 --> 00:17:20,666
The current amount you have borrowed from our bank,

222
00:17:20,726 --> 00:17:23,536
including interest, is a total of 87,000 dollars.

223
00:17:25,496 --> 00:17:28,006
Yes. I apologize. I was busy with work.

224
00:17:28,636 --> 00:17:29,836
But still...

225
00:17:30,276 --> 00:17:32,706
Isn't it a bit much to put a bank levy on me?

226
00:17:32,776 --> 00:17:34,746
You have to give a person room to breathe.

227
00:17:34,806 --> 00:17:36,246
I have a lot of debt in other places too.

228
00:17:36,846 --> 00:17:39,146
If we cannot confirm your repayment by next week,

229
00:17:39,216 --> 00:17:40,616
we will also place a levy on the officetel...

230
00:17:40,686 --> 00:17:42,286
you are currently leasing.

231
00:17:42,686 --> 00:17:44,486
Someone else already put one on it.

232
00:17:44,556 --> 00:17:46,756
Do whatever you want, whether you put a levy on it or not.

233
00:17:58,836 --> 00:18:03,506
Se Na. How many times have I told you?

234
00:18:03,976 --> 00:18:08,176
With these persimmons, you have to bite into the soft part...

235
00:18:08,246 --> 00:18:12,116
- like this to really taste... - It just gets all over your mouth.

236
00:18:12,176 --> 00:18:13,916
I don't really like it, Grandma.

237
00:18:14,246 --> 00:18:16,246
I told you we should just have ice cream.

238
00:18:17,556 --> 00:18:20,456
Kids these days don't know how to eat good food.

239
00:18:20,526 --> 00:18:22,356
Oh, you poor things.

240
00:18:25,726 --> 00:18:27,926
- Hey, Cha Se Na! - What?

241
00:18:27,996 --> 00:18:30,796
Oh my, Do Yun, I thought you had the day off today.

242
00:18:30,866 --> 00:18:32,396
Where have you been?

243
00:18:32,996 --> 00:18:34,636
Yes, Grandma, I went to the department store.

244
00:18:34,636 --> 00:18:35,636
What?

245
00:18:35,636 --> 00:18:37,806
- I need to see you. - You are looking at me right now.

246
00:18:37,876 --> 00:18:39,846
I mean I need to see you privately on the second floor.

247
00:18:39,946 --> 00:18:42,506
No, if you have something to say, say it here.

248
00:18:43,516 --> 00:18:44,816
Are you sure?

249
00:18:44,876 --> 00:18:47,216
- Don't regret it. - No, not at all.

250
00:18:52,686 --> 00:18:54,956
My goodness. What is that?

251
00:18:55,026 --> 00:18:57,926
Oh my. Oh, how hideous.

252
00:18:58,226 --> 00:19:01,066
Why are you carrying something like this around, Do Yun?

253
00:19:01,366 --> 00:19:04,066
Se Na put it in my pocket, Grandma.

254
00:19:04,136 --> 00:19:05,136
What?

255
00:19:05,196 --> 00:19:08,036
Do you know how humiliated I was at the department store today?

256
00:19:09,636 --> 00:19:11,436
So you are saying my artwork...

257
00:19:11,506 --> 00:19:13,176
has finally been revealed to the world?

258
00:19:13,876 --> 00:19:15,976
Wait, you mean...

259
00:19:16,446 --> 00:19:18,176
you made that, Se Na?

260
00:19:18,246 --> 00:19:20,116
- Yes, Grandma. - What?

261
00:19:20,116 --> 00:19:22,816
I really want to create an underwear brand with my name on it,

262
00:19:22,886 --> 00:19:24,056
and I am going to make it happen.

263
00:19:26,216 --> 00:19:28,356
So, what do you think, Grandma?

264
00:19:28,726 --> 00:19:31,026
You really want to try it on too, right?

265
00:19:31,096 --> 00:19:33,766
Well, aside from it being hideous,

266
00:19:34,096 --> 00:19:37,136
who would even wear something the size of a palm?

267
00:19:38,196 --> 00:19:40,066
These days, women wear this kind of underwear...

268
00:19:40,066 --> 00:19:41,636
for their own satisfaction.

269
00:19:42,206 --> 00:19:43,376
Am I right, Do Yun?

270
00:19:43,936 --> 00:19:45,406
I don't even want to exchange...

271
00:19:45,936 --> 00:19:47,646
a single word with you right now.

272
00:19:48,006 --> 00:19:49,406
When Mom and Dad get home from work,

273
00:19:49,406 --> 00:19:51,146
I'm going to tell them you're not preparing to study abroad...

274
00:19:51,146 --> 00:19:53,016
and are making trash like this. So be prepared.

275
00:19:53,076 --> 00:19:55,286
Why is making pretty underwear something to be criticized for?

276
00:19:56,486 --> 00:19:58,956
I'm going to create the Victoria's Secret of Korea.

277
00:20:01,026 --> 00:20:03,926
Right. Keep acting up like that.

278
00:20:04,226 --> 00:20:05,956
We will see who ends up regretting it.

279
00:20:08,566 --> 00:20:13,636
Oh, right, Seung Yun... Do Yun, give your brother a call.

280
00:20:13,706 --> 00:20:15,906
I need to know if he is coming tomorrow...

281
00:20:15,966 --> 00:20:17,736
or the day after tomorrow.

282
00:20:18,236 --> 00:20:19,236
Yes, Grandma.

283
00:20:28,346 --> 00:20:29,786
(Do Yun)

284
00:20:29,956 --> 00:20:31,556
Hey, Do Yun. It has been a while.

285
00:20:31,616 --> 00:20:32,786
Hey.

286
00:20:32,856 --> 00:20:34,726
Seung Yun, you stayed up all night again, didn't you?

287
00:20:34,786 --> 00:20:36,026
Your voice sounds like it.

288
00:20:36,356 --> 00:20:38,056
It's just because of the work here.

289
00:20:38,126 --> 00:20:39,256
How's Grandma?

290
00:20:39,326 --> 00:20:41,496
She is right next to me. Hold on.

291
00:20:41,566 --> 00:20:42,726
- Grandma, it's Seung Yun. - Okay.

292
00:20:42,726 --> 00:20:45,566
- Gosh. - Grandma, it's me, Seung Yun.

293
00:20:45,636 --> 00:20:47,836
Oh, my, my eldest grandson.

294
00:20:47,906 --> 00:20:50,636
Oh, it is my precious eldest grandson.

295
00:20:50,706 --> 00:20:52,876
So, have you eaten?

296
00:20:52,876 --> 00:20:53,906
Of course.

297
00:20:53,976 --> 00:20:56,946
Grandma, you know I get really angry if I skip even a single meal.

298
00:20:57,016 --> 00:20:58,016
You know that very well.

299
00:20:59,416 --> 00:21:00,946
Seung Yun.

300
00:21:01,286 --> 00:21:02,386
Yes, Grandma.

301
00:21:02,646 --> 00:21:04,286
When are you coming?

302
00:21:04,686 --> 00:21:07,986
I'm asking because I want to go meet you at the airport.

303
00:21:08,156 --> 00:21:09,826
I arrive the day after tomorrow, Grandma.

304
00:21:09,886 --> 00:21:12,256
You get motion sickness, Grandma, so please don't come out.

305
00:21:12,326 --> 00:21:14,296
Just rest comfortably at home, and as soon as I arrive,

306
00:21:14,366 --> 00:21:16,096
I will go see you as fast as I can.

307
00:21:16,166 --> 00:21:19,196
Will you be able to find your way home by yourself?

308
00:21:19,266 --> 00:21:21,766
Come on, Grandma, is Seung Yun a child?

309
00:21:22,106 --> 00:21:24,076
I am sure Mom will send a car for him.

310
00:21:25,906 --> 00:21:27,476
Se Na, tell your mom...

311
00:21:27,976 --> 00:21:30,276
not to come out to meet me. Tell her I will take a taxi.

312
00:21:30,746 --> 00:21:32,846
- What? Why a taxi? - What?

313
00:21:33,016 --> 00:21:34,416
Seung Yun, knowing my mom's personality,

314
00:21:34,486 --> 00:21:36,416
she will never do as you say.

315
00:21:36,486 --> 00:21:39,386
And the person looking forward to your return the most,

316
00:21:39,456 --> 00:21:41,126
next to Grandma, is my mom.

317
00:21:41,586 --> 00:21:42,726
Yes, that is right.

318
00:21:43,496 --> 00:21:44,496
Right.

319
00:21:45,896 --> 00:21:47,296
Seung Yun.

320
00:21:47,366 --> 00:21:50,296
Yes, Grandma. When I return,

321
00:21:50,366 --> 00:21:52,136
is there anything else besides cheesecake I can get for you?

322
00:21:52,666 --> 00:21:54,766
Grandma already has everything she needs.

323
00:21:55,866 --> 00:21:57,306
Seung Yun, for my gift...

324
00:21:57,306 --> 00:21:59,376
A scarf.

325
00:21:59,406 --> 00:22:02,376
A scarf? You want a scarf, Grandma?

326
00:22:02,576 --> 00:22:06,916
Get me a silk scarf with small floral patterns.

327
00:22:07,346 --> 00:22:12,156
Your father, Jun Sung, used to love it when I wore a scarf.

328
00:22:12,216 --> 00:22:15,486
He'd always say how pretty his mom looked.

329
00:22:17,696 --> 00:22:20,396
Yes, Grandma. I'll buy you the prettiest one.

330
00:22:20,466 --> 00:22:22,696
Make sure you eat well.

331
00:22:22,766 --> 00:22:24,036
I'll see you the day after tomorrow, Grandma.

332
00:22:25,466 --> 00:22:26,466
I love you.

333
00:22:26,966 --> 00:22:29,206
Okay. Oh, my sweet boy.

334
00:22:29,406 --> 00:22:31,476
Yes, my eldest grandson.

335
00:22:34,676 --> 00:22:36,716
You must be thrilled, Grandma.

336
00:22:36,946 --> 00:22:38,576
You're always rapping about...

337
00:22:38,646 --> 00:22:39,876
"my eldest grandson" and "my Seung Yun."

338
00:22:41,016 --> 00:22:42,586
Yes, of course I am.

339
00:22:43,616 --> 00:22:46,656
You are all my beautiful grandchildren,

340
00:22:46,856 --> 00:22:50,196
but the eldest grandson is different.

341
00:22:51,126 --> 00:22:54,966
He is the central root and the pillar of this family.

342
00:22:56,026 --> 00:22:58,566
So, what does that make us? Twigs?

343
00:22:58,636 --> 00:22:59,696
What?

344
00:23:00,136 --> 00:23:04,736
How can leaves grow and bear fruit without twigs?

345
00:23:09,606 --> 00:23:12,646
Grandma, go inside and lie down. I'll make the bed for you.

346
00:23:15,286 --> 00:23:16,756
Throw that away right now, got it?

347
00:23:16,816 --> 00:23:18,886
- Let's go. Okay. Oh, my. - Grandma.

348
00:23:20,526 --> 00:23:21,556
Do Yun.

349
00:23:28,566 --> 00:23:31,566
Guys, did you hear what Grandma just said?

350
00:23:32,866 --> 00:23:34,466
She called me a twig.

351
00:23:35,836 --> 00:23:38,006
Even though I'm just a twig in this house,

352
00:23:38,136 --> 00:23:40,546
I'll be a strong root and pillar for you.

353
00:23:41,846 --> 00:23:43,346
Just wait a little bit.

354
00:24:02,396 --> 00:24:04,296
(Jeon Jin Hee)

355
00:24:12,636 --> 00:24:14,576
(Jeon Jin Hee)

356
00:24:47,676 --> 00:24:48,776
This is just the beginning.

357
00:24:51,646 --> 00:24:54,786
(24 years ago)

358
00:25:31,886 --> 00:25:33,656
I will uncover the truth.

359
00:25:58,616 --> 00:25:59,816
Did you wait long?

360
00:25:59,876 --> 00:26:01,146
I'm sorry, Mi Seon.

361
00:26:01,146 --> 00:26:03,886
I was closing out the register, but the numbers kept being off.

362
00:26:03,956 --> 00:26:06,926
How have you been, Da Mi? You're right on time.

363
00:26:06,986 --> 00:26:08,026
Have some tea.

364
00:26:08,856 --> 00:26:12,696
- I was going to buy it for you. - It's the thought that counts.

365
00:26:12,826 --> 00:26:16,226
I know how much you hate spending money in places like this,

366
00:26:16,296 --> 00:26:17,696
you penny-pincher.

367
00:26:18,196 --> 00:26:20,566
Well, we've lived as a family for a long time.

368
00:26:21,366 --> 00:26:23,776
I think spending money on coffee and tea...

369
00:26:23,776 --> 00:26:25,176
is the biggest waste of money in the world.

370
00:26:25,606 --> 00:26:27,906
And then taxi fare. Right?

371
00:26:29,246 --> 00:26:31,476
You tremble over a single dollar.

372
00:26:32,676 --> 00:26:34,716
You're so different from Su Ah's dad.

373
00:26:35,986 --> 00:26:37,216
That's a relief.

374
00:26:37,856 --> 00:26:41,556
He's a bit generous and affectionate.

375
00:26:41,686 --> 00:26:43,586
Not affectionate, just careless.

376
00:26:43,926 --> 00:26:45,126
Even when you're broke.

377
00:26:45,656 --> 00:26:47,396
You fought with Gang Nam, didn't you?

378
00:26:47,626 --> 00:26:49,696
That's why neither of you came to Mom's birthday.

379
00:26:58,176 --> 00:26:59,306
Da Mi.

380
00:26:59,736 --> 00:27:02,346
- Yes? - Su Ah's dad and I...

381
00:27:02,946 --> 00:27:04,076
got divorced.

382
00:27:12,056 --> 00:27:14,086
What did you just say?

383
00:27:15,026 --> 00:27:16,286
You did what?

384
00:27:16,996 --> 00:27:17,996
We got divorced.

385
00:27:19,796 --> 00:27:21,066
We split up.

386
00:27:30,836 --> 00:27:33,636
(Mission: Mompossible)

387
00:27:33,706 --> 00:27:36,606
Mom, I am going to be 40 soon.

388
00:27:36,676 --> 00:27:38,746
Please stop hitting me. It really hurts.

389
00:27:39,076 --> 00:27:42,246
You blew your money, got divorced, and dare to say that?

390
00:27:42,386 --> 00:27:43,716
You little punk.

391
00:27:43,786 --> 00:27:45,986
- Are you sure it will be okay? - About what?

392
00:27:46,056 --> 00:27:47,356
Being in the same neighbourhood,

393
00:27:47,356 --> 00:27:50,556
you are bound to run into each other.

394
00:27:51,226 --> 00:27:54,996
Kang Da Mi, my one and only sister, please lend me 200,000 dollars.

395
00:27:55,166 --> 00:27:56,526
Did you just say 200,000 dollars?

396
00:27:56,596 --> 00:27:58,836
Not 200 dollars, not 2,000 dollars, but 200,000 dollars?

397
00:27:59,066 --> 00:28:00,366
Hey! Are you nuts?

398
00:28:04,006 --> 00:28:05,836
(Mission: Mompossible)
